      "dom_id": "question-29652",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "What is the antiderivative of $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{7}}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by writing the root as a rational power, $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{7}}={x}^{7/5}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{7}{5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{7}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{7/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{7/5+1}}{(\\frac{7}{5}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{12/5}}{(\\frac{12}{5})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{12/5}}{12}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5{x}^{12/5}}{12}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5{x}^{12/5}}{12})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{12}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{12/5})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{12}\\cdot \\frac{12}{5}{x}^{12/5-1} & = \\\\ {x}^{7/5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
